     default 30000
     help
-      While the user is active and a link exists (BLE connected / USB
-      configured), the watchdog stops being fed when either a HID send has
-      failed and no report has gone out for this long, or reports have been
-      stuck in the BLE send queues for this long. This catches a wedged hog
-      work queue, Bluetooth stack or USB stack, and the watchdog then resets
-      the MCU. Normal typing pauses do not trigger this.
+      While the selected transport is connected, stop feeding if an
+      outstanding BLE report makes no progress for this long (including
+      a blocked send call), or a USB send fails without a later success.
+      Keep checking during the hardware watchdog grace period so a
+      disconnect or recovered transmission can resume feeding. A normal
+      held key or typing pause with no outstanding send does not trigger
+      this timeout; a pending final release is monitored even after idle.
 
 config ZMK_SLEEP
     bool "Enable deep sleep support"
